<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reginald's Tower</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reginald's Tower is a round stone tower on the quay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a>, Ireland, at the apex of the old walled town. Tradition links it to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> fortification of the 10th or 11th century, though the present building is mainly Anglo-Norman work of the 12th and 13th centuries. It is regarded as the oldest civic building in Ireland and now houses a museum of Viking Waterford.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reginalds-tower.jpg" alt="Reginald's Tower" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nmwalsh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reginalds_Tower_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
